        "original_id": "26d4731a-af33-53ea-8d1c-168b7f72b04a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Columbia University, University of Colorado system, Harvard Law School, United States District Court for the District of Montana\n- People: Robert Cunningham Humphreys, Kurt Alme, Charles C. Lovell\n- Places: Upper Manhattan, New York City, Colorado, Denver, Aurora\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754.\n- Columbia University is officially named Columbia University in the City of New York.\n- Columbia University is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Columbia University is often cited as one of the world's most prestigious universities.\n- Robert Cunningham Humphreys was a student at Columbia University from 1926 to 1927.\n- The University of Colorado system is a system of public universities in Colorado.\n- The University of Colorado system consists of four campuses: the University of Colorado Boulder, the University of Colorado Colorado Springs, the University of Colorado Denver in downtown Denver, and the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora.\n- Kurt Alme graduated from the University of Colorado and Harvard Law School.\n- Kurt Alme clerked for Charles C. Lovell of the United States District Court for the District of Montana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
